bench/results/
PRIVATE_NOTES.md
docs/SPEC_single_model_integration.md

# Exam answer keys MUST NOT live in the repo: reviewing panels are dispatched
# with Bash/Read/Grep/Glob, so a key co-located with its target is discoverable
# by a single ls (precision 1.0, recall 1.0). Keys live outside the working
# tree at a location outside this tree (2026-07-29).
*_answer_key.json

# Exam review targets are NOT version-controlled — see targets/MANIFEST.md.
# A target under version control leaks itself: repairing a seeded claim touches
# only seeded claims, so `git diff` returns the planted set at precision 1.000
# with no key and nothing for a detector to catch. Hashes are committed instead.
bench/cdsfl_registry/targets/exp*.md

# ── Run logs: bulk model output is archived separately (2026-08-13) ──────────
# Measured on main before this rule: bench/logs was 353 MB across 5,840 files,
# 96.8% of the repository by size and 86% of its files. The project itself is
# ~11 MB in ~900 files. That imbalance is why external readers and crawlers
# could not navigate the repository: an unauthenticated GitHub API caller gets
# 60 requests per hour and exhausts them inside bench/logs.
#
# The split is by role, not by size:
#   KEPT   — final reports and runner_state.json. These carry the registries,
#            falsifiers and verdicts: the evidence a reader needs to check any
#            claim the project makes. 13.4 MB in 76 files.
#   DROPPED— raw per-model responses, checkpoints, debug logs, shadow traces.
#            The raw responses are primary source material and are preserved in
#            the separate archive, not discarded.
#
# This rule stops FUTURE growth only. Files already tracked stay tracked until
# the archive is published; nothing is removed from the repository before its
# replacement exists.
bench/logs/**
!bench/logs/**/
!bench/logs/**/*report*.json
!bench/logs/**/runner_state.json
